WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.334
And finally, over the weekend, crypto exchange company FTX

00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:04.968
crashed and filed for bankruptcy.

00:00:04.968 --> 00:00:07.100
Here with more on that is "Late Night" writer

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:08.901
and financial expert Jeff Wright.

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.634 --> 00:00:17.501
-Thank you. Thank you, Seth.

00:00:17.501 --> 00:00:20.701
FTX is melting down, and I just want to comfort investors

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:24.667
out there by saying I told you so, okay?

00:00:24.667 --> 00:00:28.734
Crypto is stupid, and we Black people never trusted it.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:31.968
-So why do you think Black people never trusted it?

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.300
-Well, first of all, we are naturally skeptical

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.067
about everything a white man tells us.

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.234
For example, when you hired me to be on the show,

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:41.667
I thought you were playin'.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:45.601
I'm so paranoid, I still don't know if I really work here.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.434
Matter of fact, I never unpacked.

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:49.968
My bags are right there.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.434
-That's ridiculous, Jeff.

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:53.601
You've been here for two years now.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:56.501
-Ah, interesting. You're really keeping track, aren't you?

00:00:56.501 --> 00:00:58.567
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.567 --> 00:01:02.400
Anyways, we don't trust crypto because it's inconsistent.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.667
Black people only recently started getting money

00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:06.734
and building wealth in our own communities,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:07.934
and what did white people do?

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.234
Went and changed what money was.

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.434
Just created a whole new currency!

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:17.234
You can't create a new game when we just learned this one!

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:20.968
It's like the makers of Uno coming out with the game Dos.

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:24.367
Why would you do that

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.934
when some people don't know how to play Uno the right way?

00:01:27.934 --> 00:01:31.367
-You can't put a Draw 4 on a Draw 4!

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.901
-Yes, you can, Seth!

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.734
-No! -That's how you play!

00:01:35.734 --> 00:01:38.033
-No, you cannot do that!

00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:39.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.701 --> 00:01:42.334
Anyway, as a financial expert, what do you suggest other

00:01:42.334 --> 00:01:45.601
crypto exchange companies do to avoid their own demise?

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:48.901
-Well, first, we got to change the name of crypto.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.067
You can't say, "We made this new money,

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.567
and it's totally safe and easy to understand,"

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:56.167
and then call it "crypto."

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.667
I mean, listen to it. Crypto.

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.400
That sounds less like money

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:04.234
and more like the new dance craze in Compton, California.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:05.901
I could just picture someone going, "Hey,

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:09.834
show your auntie that new crypto dance y'all been doing."

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:12.400
Second, you've got to make the currencies themselves

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:14.300
sound less crazy.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.701
Back in the day, you invested

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:18.200
in things like Apple, Google, Microsoft.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.834
Nowadays, you got people investing in Ethereum.

00:02:20.834 --> 00:02:23.400
What the hell is an Ethereum?

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.834
First time I heard of it,

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:27.834
I thought it was a new house in "Harry Potter."

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.467
Someone asked me, "Hey, man, you on that Ethereum?"

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:33.400
I was like, "No. The BuzzFeed quiz said I was a Slytherin."

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.968
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.968 --> 00:02:37.834
-Now, Jeff, what would you tell everyday investors

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:39.601
who are, you know, looking to make a profit?

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:43.400
-Well, first, I would tell them listen to Black people, okay?

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.601
We've never been wrong.

00:02:45.601 --> 00:02:48.901
And even when we were, we would never admit it.

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.033
Secondly, if you don't know how to spell it or where it's from,

00:02:52.033 --> 00:02:53.901
don't buy it, okay?

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.367
Lastly, but more importantly,

00:02:56.367 --> 00:02:58.868
stop listening to your dumb-ass friends, okay?

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.501
Just because they bought a little bit of Bitcoin

00:03:01.501 --> 00:03:03.834
does not mean they're a Wall Street day trader.

00:03:03.834 --> 00:03:05.767
My friend Sean bought a little bit of Bitcoin.

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:07.968
Now he wears a business suit and a earpiece.

00:03:07.968 --> 00:03:11.834
He started using words like "diversify" and "portfolio."

00:03:11.834 --> 00:03:13.801
You still work at Subway, Sean!

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:15.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:20.467
-Give it up for our financial expert, Jeff Wright, everybody!

